public sealed class HomesConfig { public int MaxHomes { get; set; } = 3; public int CooldownSeconds { get; set; } = 5; }
[JsonSerializable(typeof(HomesConfig))] partial class Json : JsonSerializerContext;
var config = Config.Load(Json.Default.HomesConfig);   // config.Value.MaxHomes

member.summary:
An NBT value (the data format of block entities, entities, item components and level data). Tags are mutable managed objects: they are
            copies of the engine's data, so changing one changes nothing in the world until it is handed back (for example to
            ). Use  for a deep copy.

The system's effective registry name: the requested one (namespaced by the plugin, see
            ), or, while a hot-reload predecessor still holds that name, the
            temporary "name#2" form. Renamed back to the plain name once the predecessor is released.

Changes a block, like /setblock: the old block entity goes away, the new block's placement logic and the neighbour updates run (per
            ), the clients are told. No player event fires (this is not a player placing the block); the engine's own block events (a fire spreading,
            a piston moving) are the ones the block triggers itself.
